data.content:
## What Breaks in .NET 11

In .NET 10, the Cosmos DB provider removed native sync support but offered a **sync-over-async opt-in** (e.g., `CosmosOptionsExtension` with `EnableSyncOverAsync()`). In .NET 11, **that opt-in is removed entirely**.

All synchronous LINQ operators — `ToList()`, `First()`, `Count()`, and `SaveChanges()` — will throw an **`InvalidOperationException`** at runtime because the Cosmos provider has no sync execution path.

## The Fix

You must convert to async equivalents:

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

**Key changes:**
1. Return `Task<T>` / `Task` instead of sync types
2. Replace `ToList()` → `ToListAsync()`, `First()` → `FirstAsync()`, `Count()` → `CountAsync()`, `SaveChanges()` → `SaveChangesAsync()`
3. Callers up the chain must also become `async`/`await`

There is no workaround — the Cosmos provider is async-only in .NET 11.
